cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to Saboot in research, teaching or legal-aid work, please cite it as below."
title: "Saboot: offline helper for the section 63(4) Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam electronic evidence certificate"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: byjoellobo
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/byjoellobo/saboot"
url: "https://byjoellobo.github.io/saboot/"
abstract: >-
  Saboot is an offline-first web app that hashes electronic evidence (WhatsApp
  chat exports, screenshots, call recordings and CCTV footage) on the user's own
  device, guides them to the identifiers of the source device, and drafts the
  certificate required by section 63(4) of the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam,
  2023, with a hash report, QR verification and a per-message hashed WhatsApp
  transcript. It is not legal advice.
keywords:
  - electronic evidence
  - Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam
  - section 63
  - hash
  - SHA-256
  - WhatsApp
  - access to justice
  - India
